241 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (The Demogorgon residence is conceived as a living subterranean biome where architecture, geology, and biology function as a single integrated system. By embedding itself within fractured basalt, fungal networks, geothermal cavities, and existing cave systems, the shelter becomes an extension of the Upside Down itself. Instead of altering the landscape, it reinforces the natural processes already present, providing concealment, thermal stability, moisture, protection, and rapid access to hunting territories. The result is a habitat that enhances the survival, reproduction, and territorial behavior of Demogorgons while remaining inseparable from its environment.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [26]
>>
